,"unit_id":"u15"},{"reason":"Heading for a separate dealing control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u16"},{"reason":"Observed redemption restrictions concern a separate control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Fairness and redemption requirements are outside the selected gift control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u18"},{"reason":"Administrative procedures and best-endeavours language concern dealing frequency, not a gift exception.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u19"},{"reason":"Heading for separate marketing requirements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u20"},{"reason":"Misleading-information requirement is independently applicable context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u21"},{"reason":"Advertising-guideline dependency concerns financial-return presentation.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u22"},{"reason":"Risk and deposit-comparison restrictions are separate marketing controls.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u23"},{"reason":"Monitoring and possible regulatory action do not supply a commencement date or automatic sanction for this control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u24"},{"reason":"Departmental attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u25"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u26"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u27"},{"reason":"Offering-document authority supports u11; not an additional condition of the selected control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u28"},{"reason":"Identifies the Code and its licensed-or-registered-person framing; full applicability remains unresolved.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u29"},{"reason":"Identifies the FAQ supporting the product-type connection and its issuance date; the answer itself is absent.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u30"},{"reason":"Referenced advertising supplements are absent and concern a separate control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u31"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The circular defines distributors through SFC-authorised fund distribution, while u14 states the control using generic investment-product language. Readings R1 and R2 distinguish a general product rule for those distributors from a rule confined here to their SFC-authorised fund promotions. Neither reading requires public advertising, an online platform or proven distraction.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u5","u14","u15","u29"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Gift is not exhaustively defined. Guaranteed returns and other incentives may qualify, rather than qualifying automatically. Product types expressly include certain fund types and funds from certain fund houses. The boundaries of gift, discount and promotional linkage require judgment.","source_unit_ids":["u8","u13","u14"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The fee-or-charge discount parenthesis attaches to gifts. It does not exempt an entire mixed promotion or disapply separate advertising rules. The text supplies no authority for treating every rebate or return enhancement as a discount, and supplies no de minimis exception.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u14","u15"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The selected standard is expressed as should not offer, reinforced by will be bound. May be considered preserves uncertainty in gift classification. The proposed Boolean outcome identifies a departure from that selected standard, not a statutory offence or an automatic enforcement outcome.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u24"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The packet supplies no commencement date, transition or deadline for the gift control. The date 2010-09-30 identifies the referenced FAQ’s issuance, not this control’s commencement. Temporal applicability cannot be resolved from the retained text.","source_unit_ids":["u14","u24","u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"Paragraph 3.11 and FAQ question 1 are referenced but their full texts and applicable versions are unavailable. The external-authorities.23ec46 dependency is unresolved. Section 103, disclosure, dealing and advertising provisions remain separate; satisfying the gift control cannot establish compliance with them.","source_unit_ids":["u7","u10","u12","u15","u18","u21","u22","u28","u29","u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the applicable paragraph 3.11 extend this statement to all investment-product promotions by the relevant distributor, or is this circular’s selected application confined to SFC-authorised funds?","What do the applicable Code and FAQ question 1 say about gift classification, promotional linkage, cash rebates and discounts of fees or charges?","Which versions and effective dates of the referenced authorities govern the assessed offer?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["Assess one identified benefit offered by one actor in one promotion to one client; assess distinct benefits separately.","The actor is assessed using u1’s distributor definition. Coverage of persons who do not distribute SFC-authorised funds is unresolved.","A qualifying discount excludes that benefit only. A separate non-discount gift in the same promotion remains independently assessable.","Actual investor distraction is the stated rationale, not an additional factual prerequisite.","The formalization is a conditional reading of the retained standard; it does not establish temporal applicability or resolve missing authorities."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct provides that distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement as investors may be distracted from the unique features and risks of such particular funds3.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"2 The Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission (Code of Conduct).","unit_id":"u29"}],"distinction":"R1 gives operative weight to u14’s generic investment-product wording. For a distributor within u1, an otherwise qualifying gift linked to a non-fund investment product is within this selected reading. R2 excludes that case from its scope. The strongest uncertainty is whether the circular is restating the Code’s general reach or only describing its fund-specific application.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary that distributes SFC-authorised funds, within the distributor description in u1.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed promotion concerns an SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of SFC-authorised fund.","name":"is_authorised_fund_promotion","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u14","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The actor offers the identified benefit to a client in the assessed promotion; delivery or acceptance is not required.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift for the selected paragraph 3.11 control, before applying the discount exception; an incentive or guaranteed return does not establish this automatically.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the stated exception.","name":"benefit_is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The benefit is offered in promoting a specific investment product or a particular investment-product type, including a type connection established by how the benefit is offered; examples include certain fund types or funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14","u30"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_offered_to_client benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount) has_product_promotion_connection)","result_type":"bool","scope":"is_distributor"},"local_id":"gift_scope_r1","questions":["Does u14’s generic investment-product wording govern promotions beyond SFC-authorised funds by a distributor defined in u1?","How does the full Code determine actor coverage beyond the circular’s distributor definition?"],"statement":"Selected control: paragraph-10 gift-offer restriction, general-product reading. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, if the intermediary offers a client a benefit that qualifies as a gift, the benefit is not a discount of fees or charges, and its offer promotes a specific investment product or a particular investment-product type, the offer departs from the stated should-not-offer standard. A product-type connection includes the specified fund-category and fund-house connections. Structured-product status and proof of actual distraction are not prerequisites. Within scope, a true formal result flags that departure; a false result addresses only this selected benefit and control.","subject":"Paragraph-10 gift-promotion control"},{"assumptions":["Assess one identified benefit offered by one actor in one promotion to one client; assess distinct benefits separately.","Read the generic wording in u14 within the circular’s SFC-authorised-fund subject matter.","A qualifying discount excludes that benefit only. A separate non-discount gift in the same promotion remains independently assessable.","Actual investor distraction is the stated rationale, not an additional factual prerequisite.","The formalization is a conditional reading of the retained standard; it does not establish temporal applicability or resolve missing authorities."],"citations":[{"quote":"This circular summarises the Securities and Futures Commission’s (SFC) recent observations of licensed corporations’ practices in offering and promoting SFC-authorised funds.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO, distributors are reminded to have regard to paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct provides that distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"when offering or promoting funds, distributors should not offer additional returns","unit_id":"u15"},{"quote":"3 The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.","unit_id":"u30"}],"distinction":"R2 limits the application established by this circular to SFC-authorised fund promotions, while retaining every operative gift condition and the discount exception. A promotion of another investment product falls outside this selected formal scope, without implying permission under the Code. Its strongest weakness is u14’s unqualified reference to investment products rather than only funds.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary that distributes SFC-authorised funds, within the distributor description in u1.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed promotion concerns an SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of SFC-authorised fund.","name":"is_authorised_fund_promotion","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u14","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The actor offers the identified benefit to a client in the assessed promotion; delivery or acceptance is not required.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift for the selected paragraph 3.11 control, before applying the discount exception; an incentive or guaranteed return does not establish this automatically.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the stated exception.","name":"benefit_is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The benefit is offered in promoting a specific investment product or a particular investment-product type, including a type connection established by how the benefit is offered; examples include certain fund types or funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14","u30"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_offered_to_client benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount) has_product_promotion_connection)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor is_authorised_fund_promotion)"},"local_id":"gift_scope_r2","questions":["Does the fund-focused context limit the application stated here despite u14’s generic wording?","Does the referenced FAQ clarify whether a broad fund-platform promotion has the required product-type connection?"],"statement":"Selected control: paragraph-10 gift-offer restriction, fund-context reading. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, assess this restriction when the promotion concerns an SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of such fund. If the intermediary offers a client a gift, the gift is not a discount of fees or charges, and its offer has the specified product or product-type promotional connection, the offer departs from the stated should-not-offer standard. Fund-house groupings can supply that connection. Structured-product status and proof of actual distraction are not prerequisites. Within scope, a true formal result flags that departure; other products are outside this reading’s selected scope, with their treatment under the full Code unresolved.","subject":"Paragraph-10 gift-promotion control"}]},"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines distributors and the circular’s SFC-authorised-fund setting; informs competing scope readings.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Observed additional features and restrictions explain the circular’s setting.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Standing-instruction services provide context, not an independent gift-control trigger.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Marketing observations do not limit the selected control to public or aggressive campaigns.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Guaranteed-returns heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Identifies the separate statutory provision; its complete text is unavailable.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Describes guaranteed-return components without conclusively classifying them as gifts.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Conditional structured-product classification belongs to a separate control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Separate public-invitation offence and its authorisation/exemption conditions; these exceptions are not imported into the gift control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Disclosure and misleading-impression concerns provide context; separate obligations are not formalized.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies paragraph 3.11 as the selected control’s referenced authority.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Gift classification remains conditional, and the gift control can apply even without structured-product status.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"Principal selected provision: actor, gift prohibition, discount exception, and product or product-type connection.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Connects additional returns and incentives to the two separate controls without making every incentive a breach.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u15"},{"reason":"Separate dealing-restrictions heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u16"},{"reason":"Observed dealing restrictions provide surrounding context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Fairness and redemption obligations are outside the selected gift control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u18"},{"reason":"Administrative procedures and best-endeavours dealing obligations are outside the selected control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u19"},{"reason":"Separate marketing heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u20"},{"reason":"Misleading-advertisement duties and paragraph 2.3 require separate analysis.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u21"},{"reason":"Advertising Guidelines dependency belongs to a separate advertising control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u22"},{"reason":"Risk and deposit-comparison restrictions are separate advertising controls.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u23"},{"reason":"Monitoring and possible regulatory action provide enforcement context, not an effective date or automatic sanction.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u24"},{"reason":"Departmental attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u25"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u26"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u27"},{"reason":"Footnote identifies a separate offering-document requirement and unavailable Handbook dependency.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u28"},{"reason":"Identifies the Code’s title and supports consideration of licensed or registered persons; does not establish any particular actor’s status.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u29"},{"reason":"Identifies the FAQ supporting product-type linkage and its issue date; the answer itself is unavailable.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u30"},{"reason":"Unspecified supplementary advertising guidance remains an external dependency.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u31"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The circular defines distributors by distribution of SFC-authorised funds, while its account of paragraph 3.11 uses investment-product language. The competing readings differ on whether this selected control extends to those distributors’ promotions of other investment products.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u14","u15","u29"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Additional returns and incentives may constitute gifts; the text does not make that classification automatic. Product-type linkage expressly includes certain fund types and funds from certain fund houses. Gift, discount, and the full limits of linkage remain undefined.","source_unit_ids":["u8","u13","u14"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The fee-or-charge discount exception attaches to gifts in the selected control. Section 103 authorisation or exemption is a separate exception and does not excuse a gift-control failure. Whether rebates or mixed benefits qualify as discounts remains unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u14","u15"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The selected provision says distributors should not offer gifts; it is modeled as a selected conduct-control screen, without equating it to the separate statutory offence. The phrase may be considered preserves judgment about gift classification; actual investor distraction is not stated as a necessary condition.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u15","u24"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"30 September 2010 dates the referenced FAQ’s issuance, not commencement of this circular or the selected control. No circular issue date, effective date, transition period, or applicable Code version is supplied.","source_unit_ids":["u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The complete paragraph 3.11 and FAQ question 1 answer are needed to resolve scope and classification. The packet identifies external-authorities.23ec46 without supplying its contents or hash. Other statutory, Handbook, and advertising dependencies remain separate.","source_unit_ids":["u7","u10","u12","u14","u28","u29","u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the complete paragraph 3.11 establish investment-product-wide application to the actors concerned, or should this retained circular be used only for SFC-authorised-fund promotions?","What does the referenced FAQ answer say about indirect links, fund-house groupings, and promotions spanning multiple product types?","Which additional returns or incentives count as gifts, and when do cash rebates, third-party fee reductions, or mixed benefits qualify as discounts of fees or charges?","What circular date, Code version, FAQ version, and effective-date provisions govern the proposed assessment?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The assessment concerns one identified offer or proposed offer to a client.","The circular’s defined distributor category supplies actor scope, but the quoted investment-product wording supplies product scope.","The Boolean result is a selected paragraph-10 gift-control pass only when scope is true; it does not establish overall compliance.","Gift classification and promotional linkage are supplied judgments, not inferred truth values."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"}],"distinction":"For an intermediary within the circular’s distributor category, this reading also screens a promotion of an investment product outside SFC-authorised funds. The strongest uncertainty is whether the circular’s quotation supplies that broader application without the complete Code provision.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the circular’s distributor category.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed activity promotes a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to a client, including a substantively linked gift arrangement of the kind described in u14.","name":"has_product_promotion_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed promotion concerns SFC-authorised funds.","name":"promotes_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed offer includes a benefit classified as a gift for the selected control, before applying the discount exception.","name":"offers_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Every gift component in the assessed offer qualifies as a discount of fees or charges; any non-discount gift component makes this false.","name":"all_gifts_are_fee_discounts","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(or (not offers_gift) all_gifts_are_fee_discounts)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor has_product_promotion_link)"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["Does paragraph 3.11’s full actor and product scope support extending this screen to the distributor’s other investment-product promotions?"],"statement":"Read the investment-product wording in paragraph 10 as stating a general gift-promotion control for the identified distributors: a gift linked to promotion of a specific investment product or product type to a client fails this selected control unless it is a discount of fees or charges. Neither structured-product classification nor proof of actual distraction is an additional trigger.","subject":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control with investment-product-wide scope"},{"assumptions":["The assessment concerns one identified offer or proposed offer to a client.","The circular’s SFC-authorised-fund setting limits the application established by this retained text; wider Code application remains unresolved.","The Boolean result is a selected paragraph-10 gift-control pass only when scope is true; an out-of-scope offer is not thereby permitted.","Gift classification and promotional linkage use the same meanings as in r1."],"citations":[{"quote":"This circular summarises the Securities and Futures Commission’s (SFC) recent observations of licensed corporations’ practices in offering and promoting SFC-authorised funds.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges)","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"when offering or promoting funds, distributors should not offer additional returns","unit_id":"u15"},{"quote":"3 The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.","unit_id":"u30"}],"distinction":"The same non-discount gift offered in promotion of another investment product is outside this retained-text screen, whereas r1 screens it. This does not establish an exemption under the Code. The strongest uncertainty is whether limiting application to the circular’s subject understates the deliberately general wording in u14.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the circular’s distributor category.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed activity promotes a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to a client, including a substantively linked gift arrangement of the kind described in u14.","name":"has_product_promotion_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed promotion concerns SFC-authorised funds.","name":"promotes_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed offer includes a benefit classified as a gift for the selected control, before applying the discount exception.","name":"offers_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Every gift component in the assessed offer qualifies as a discount of fees or charges; any non-discount gift component makes this false.","name":"all_gifts_are_fee_discounts","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(or (not offers_gift) all_gifts_are_fee_discounts)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor has_product_promotion_link promotes_authorised_funds)"},"local_id":"r2","questions":["Is the fund setting an application limit of this circular only, with broader obligations established independently by the complete Code?"],"statement":"Read paragraph 10 as applying the referenced gift rule within this circular’s SFC-authorised-fund subject. Distributors should not offer non-discount gifts linked to promoting a specific such fund or a particular fund type, including funds grouped by fund house. The retained text leaves application to other investment products for determination from the complete Code and FAQ.","subject":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control within the circular’s fund context"}]}},"java_checks":[],"live_provider":true,"model_calls":3,"no_progress":0,"nodes":[],"pending":null,"provider_id":"codex.fresh.v1","retrievals":[],"rounds":0,"roundtrips":[],"run_id":"run.43cfe1f6c26f47b89fa28eb53ba97027","stop":null}